
---

## Layer Responsibilities

### api/
- Public entry points
- Minimal surface area
- No OpenPDF imports
- No framework dependencies

Example:
- PdfTemplateEngine
- RenderResult

---

### generator/
- Core domain logic
- Template parsing and validation
- Rendering pipeline
- Business rules

Rules:
- MUST NOT depend on OpenPDF
- MUST NOT depend on file system
- MUST NOT depend on frameworks

---

### engine/
- Defines PDF engine contracts
- Abstract operations like:
  - createDocument
  - addText
  - addTable

Rules:
- Interfaces only
- No implementation logic

---

### adapter/
- Technical implementations
- Uses concrete libraries (e.g. OpenPDF)

Rules:
- MAY depend on generator + engine
- MUST NOT be referenced by generator or api

---

## Dependency Rules (STRICT)

Allowed:
- api → generator
- generator → engine
- adapter → engine
- adapter → generator

Forbidden:
- generator → adapter
- api → adapter
- api → OpenPDF
- generator → OpenPDF

Violations MUST be rejected in code review.

---

## Testing Strategy

- generator layer:
  - Unit tests only
  - No OpenPDF
- adapter layer:
  - Integration tests allowed
  - OpenPDF usage tested here

---

## Versioning Rules

- The API layer defines public compatibility
- Changes in api/ are considered breaking
- generator/ changes are internal unless exposed via api/

---

## Design Principles

- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Keep constructors explicit
- Avoid static state
- Favor immutability

---

## What NOT to do

- Do not expose OpenPDF types in api/
- Do not add framework annotations (Spring, etc.)
- Do not bypass engine ports
- Do not create "utils" with business logic

---

## AI Usage Instructions

When generating code:
- Respect the package boundaries
- Do not introduce OpenPDF into generator or api
- Keep public APIs minimal
- Prefer small, focused classes

---

## Ownership

This MDC is authoritative for Kotlin libraries in this repository.
Any deviation must be documented and justified.

io.github.<org>.core
├── api/ # Public API (stable)
├── generator/ # Core PDF generation logic (engine-agnostic)
├── engine/ # Engine ports (interfaces)
├── adapter/ # Concrete implementations (OpenPDF, etc.)
│ └── openpdf/
├── util/ # Shared utilities


